Package: slk
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/raulsh/slk
Description: Read your Slack from the command line, as you
 slk reads Slack using the credentials your own browser already holds - an
 xoxc web-client token paired with the xoxd session cookie - so it sees your
 DMs, your private channels, your unread state and your search results, and
 needs no workspace administrator to install anything.
 .
 It exists so an AI agent can shell out to a binary instead of driving a
 browser. Output is shaped for a caller that pays per token: compact records
 with names already resolved, one self-describing JSON envelope per command,
 distinct exit codes per failure cause, and nothing but results on stdout.
 There is also an interactive terminal browser for when a person would rather
 look around.
 .
 This uses Slack's internal client API, which is undocumented and
 unsupported: endpoints can change without notice, and the credentials expire
 whenever the browser session rotates. Whether you may use it on a given
 workspace is between you and that workspace's policy.
